9weo|v|To roll over, or to and fro; to throw one's self about; as, a person on pain tumbles and tosses. ; To roll down; to fall suddenly and violently; to be precipitated; as, to tumble from a scaffold. ; To play tricks by various movements and contortions of the body; to perform the feats of an acrobat. ; To turn over; to turn or throw about, as for examination or search; to roll or move in a rough, coarse, or unceremonious manner; to throw down or headlong; to precipitate; -- sometimes with over, about, etc.; as, to tumble books or papers. ; To disturb; to rumple; as, to tumble a bed.	o:9s0f,20,2~9s0f,20,2	d:599p,15,6~599p,15,6	D:1ey2,126,5;7pir,40,4;3flv,22,3;j3w,6,5~1ey2,126,5;j3w,6,5;7pir,40,4;3flv,22,3
