9wpv|n|An East Indian plant of the genus Curcuma, of the Ginger family. ; The root or rootstock of the Curcuma longa. It is externally grayish, but internally of a deep, lively yellow or saffron color, and has a slight aromatic smell, and a bitterish, slightly acrid taste. It is used for a dye, a medicine, a condiment, and a chemical test.	a:7qfl,34,2~7qfl,34,2	n:aj94,15,1~aj94,15,1	N:90hq,84,1~90hq,84,1
